# T12589 — Interoperability with RIPv1/v2 (Policy Based Routing) — tb470 IE520 stack — 2026-09-30 — PARTIAL

Verdict: PARTIAL, pending Terrence's scope decision. This run was the agreed support probe only.
Terrence expected "PBR *doesnt* exist … check anyway". It DOES exist on the IE520
(awplus_main-20260923-20): with QoS enabled, a policy-map class offers `set ip next-hop A.B.C.D`
("Set the Policy Based Routing nexthop"), and `set ip next-hop 10.10.10.2` was ACCEPTED (no `% ` line).
So the case is not UNSUPPORTED. Per the triage instruction, the full case (RIPv2/v1, two next-hop VLANs,
traffic Pkts1/Pkts2, VLAN30 down/up, invalid next-hop) was NOT built. Steps 1–5 are not run. Sent to
the sentinel at 13:37: "NEEDS TERRENCE: PBR exists — scope OK for the full 12589 build?"

Run labelled: clean (probe only; the policy-map was never attached to a port, so no traffic was affected).

Operator: bench-runner subagent (sentinel = parent session device-testing-ba, /test-mode shape A).
Queue: IE520/CAMPAIGN-QUEUE-2026-09-29.md row 14. Case text: ck.db zephyr AWPTCM-T12589, folder "/Policy
Based Routing/Policy based Routing - x510". Objective "Confirm that Policy-based Routing and RIPv1/v2 work
correctly each other". Environment and switch config are "See attachment file", and the attachment is
not in ck.db. Terrence (2026-09-30): "yes, run the probe", then "PBR *doesnt* exist. am pretty sure.
check anyway."

## Pre-case state
Same group session as T5082 (../dhcpv6-2026-09-29/5082-fail.log). Probe 2026-09-30T001909Z MATCH. The
pre-group capture is ../dhcpv6-2026-09-29/pre-test-configs/2026-09-30/pre-u{0,1,3,5}.out. The stack
running-config after T5082's teardown was IDENTICAL to it, with no `mls qos` line (QoS off). Gate items
