## Step 1 — CLI help without QoS (`?` with NO CR, qmark.py, Ctrl-U self-test passed) (evidence/12589/12589-q-*.out, 13:34–13:35)
```
(config)#policy-based-routing ?      % Unrecognized command      (the x230/AR4050 PBR enable command)
(config)#ip policy ?                 % Unrecognized command
(config)#policy-map ?                NAME  Specify a policy-map name
(config)#class-map ?                 NAME  Specify a class-map name
(config)#route-map ?                 WORD  Route map tag
(config-if vlan10)#ip policy ?       % Unrecognized command
#show policy-based-routing ?         % Unrecognized command
```
`class-map ck12589` without QoS → `% QoS is not enabled globally` (evidence/12589/12589-s1-u5.out, 13:35:27).

## Step 2 — enable QoS, scratch class-map + policy-map (13:36:06–13:36:12, evidence/12589/12589-s2-u5.out)
```
IE520-stk(config)#mls qos enable
Traffic will stop while configuration is applied. Continue? (y/n): y
IE520-stk(config)#class-map ck12589
IE520-stk(config-cmap)#exit
IE520-stk(config)#policy-map ck12589
IE520-stk(config-pmap)#class ck12589
IE520-stk(config-pmap-c)#
show stack -> members 1/3/4 Ready, member 3 Active Master, Normal operation
```

## Step 3 — the PBR probe inside the policy-map class (13:36:33–13:37:01, evidence/12589/12589-q-pmapc-u5.out, -q-pmapdef-u5.out)
```
IE520-stk(config-pmap-c)# ?
Policy map class configuration commands:
  do / exit / help / no / police / police-aggregate / set / show / storm-action / storm-downtime /
  storm-protection / storm-rate / storm-window
IE520-stk(config-pmap-c)#set ?
  bandwidth-class  Bandwidth-class
  cos              CoS
  dscp             DSCP
  ip               Change an IP routing setting
  queue            Queue
IE520-stk(config-pmap-c)#set ip ?
  next-hop  Set the Policy Based Routing nexthop
IE520-stk(config-pmap-c)#set ip next-hop ?
  A.B.C.D  Nexthop IP address
```
`class default` of the same policy-map offers the same `set ip next-hop`.

## Step 4 — the command is accepted (13:37:21–13:37:24, evidence/12589/12589-s3-u5.out)
```
IE520-stk(config-pmap-c)#set ip next-hop 10.10.10.2          (no % line)
do show running-config | include mls|class|policy|next-hop:
mls qos enable
class-map ck12589
policy-map ck12589
 class default
 class ck12589
  set ip next-hop 10.10.10.2
```
The policy-map was not attached to any port (`service-policy input`). PBR forwarding was therefore not
exercised.

## Not run — case steps 1–5 (awaiting scope)
The full case needs: RIPv2 (then v1) on "all of switches"; two egress VLANs (VLAN30 = PBR next hop,
VLAN40 = the RIP route); a class-map matching source 192.168.10.128–254; the policy-map attached on the
ingress port; and Pkts1/Pkts2 from a traffic source (tcpreplay/scapy on a tb470 NIC in place of IXIA1).
Then VLAN30 down/up and an invalid next-hop. The switch config is in an attachment that ck.db does not
hold. Unblocks with: Terrence's "scope OK" (relayed by the sentinel), then a routing-group build on the
stack with the IE520-sa and/or the AR4050S as RIP peers.

## Teardown (13:37:48–13:37:56, evidence/12589/12589-td-u5.out)
```
IE520-stk(config)#no policy-map ck12589       (no % line)
IE520-stk(config)#no class-map ck12589        (no % line)
IE520-stk(config)#no mls qos                  (no % line, and NO (y/n) prompt on this build)
```
The `no mls qos` gave no prompt, so ckyn.py stopped there as designed ("expected (y/n) but got a
prompt"). The command had taken effect: `show running-config` of the stack afterwards is IDENTICAL to the
pre-group capture (no mls/class-map/policy-map lines). Group close 13:38–13:39 (see
../dhcpv6-2026-09-29/README.md): u5/u3/u1/u0 IDENTICAL, boot config tb470-bench.cfg on all, probe
2026-09-30T003900Z MATCH.
